{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dapper multi mapping dapper multi mapping","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md","fileName":"Dapper Multi-Mapping.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dapper Multi-Mapping","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Dapper Data Access]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Dapper Data Access","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dapper multi mapping dapper multi mapping","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md","fileName":"Dapper Multi-Mapping.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dapper Multi-Mapping","heading":"Dapper Multi-Mapping","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Dapper multi-mapping divides columns from one joined row into multiple object types and uses a mapping function to assemble their relationship. It supports loading a parent and related records from one query rather than issuing a new query for every parent.\n\nBecause a join repeats parent columns for each child, the mapping code must identify existing parent objects and attach each child to the correct collection. The reduced round trips are exchanged for more deliberate assembly logic.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Dapper Data Access","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dapper Multi-Mapping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dapper multi mapping dapper multi mapping","filePath":"6 - Ful